invariant: INV-17
file: srv_quic.c
catches: quic_loop_test
reason: the server driver keeps its own copy of the old failure path and
  wipes every key, the write keys included, instead of calling quic_fail,
  so a server that fails with no_application_protocol, or on a KeyUpdate
  at the Handshake level, has no key to seal the CONNECTION_CLOSE RFC
  9001 section 4.8 asks for. test/quic_loop_close.h requires the server's
  close at every level it had keys for to seal and to open at the client.

--- old
        rc = advance(q);
        if (rc != CH_OK) {
            return quic_fail(q, rc);
        }
--- new
        rc = advance(q);
        if (rc != CH_OK) {
            q->alert = q->hs.alert;
            quic_wipe(q);
            q->t.state = CH_ST_FAILED;
            return rc;
        }
